  "patch_id": "CAM_ORCHESTRATOR_RECOVERY_EVIDENCE_001",
  "title": "docs(investigations): CAM orchestrator recovery evidence + March 2026 consolidation recovery census (evidence only)",
  "intent": "Determine whether the archived 2026-03-18 neck-CAM orchestrator is a predecessor or partial fix for the neck rapid-at-cutting-depth defect, and census what the March 15-21 consolidation period stranded. Evidence only; no production behaviour changes.",
  "change_type": "docs",
  "behavior_change": "None. No file under services/api/app, packages/client, workflows, configs or baselines is modified. Adds investigation documents, preserved offline replay outputs, three read-only evidence tools under scripts/investigations/, one test module, and one ACKNOWLEDGED_NON_DIMENSION_FILES entry in test_jumbo_dimension_consistency.py. Findings: the archived orchestrator does not touch the defect (702 rapids below Z0 on the pre-#398 tree with or without it), cannot run on the current machine contract, and duplicates tool changes; owner ruled SUPERSEDED / INCOMPATIBLE_WITH_CURRENT_RUNTIME / DO_NOT_FORWARD_PORT. The census records 52 sources, 194 candidates, and one active safety candidate (/api/headstock/transition/gcode) routed to its own order and not fixed here.",
  "risk_level": "low",
